{"request_sha256": "050cd3b8a33a4d0808a43f9cf7e2055ca6e3785630587201eab27192feb42a7e", "prompt_sha256": "41ce0317d48d66c48f27d90ac1b32c243e3040b9e4e995bf9fe78793a495333b", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "091f63615be6708985c4a014218a8c751a0b5aa510980d268c3982fbbcd9e5ed", "schema_sha256": "16e85d59e1b5b494dcb4212f6a717d121774f1597ba7eb3b65eaf0b4c9e5ff18", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 8649}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass", "pass", "pass", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": [{"defect": "Fronds are straight radiating spokes. They do not arch outward and down, so the crown outline reads as a round starburst instead of the drooping dome in reference-0 (render-0, render-1).", "trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds"}, {"defect": "Leaflets are short, small and sparse along each rachis. Each frond reads as a thin spray instead of the dense, long-leafleted plumose frond in reference-0 and reference-1, so the owner's 'too thin and short' concern is still visible.", "trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds"}, {"defect": "The lowest fronds hang straight down in a tight column against the upper trunk. They do not arch out and droop around the crown (render-0, render-2).", "trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds"}, {"defect": "The trunk is a smooth cylinder with sparse, widely spaced round-capped cylindrical pegs. There is no tessellating spiral lattice of blunt wedge stubs with flat angular faces (render-2, render-3 vs reference-1, reference-2).", "trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern"}, {"defect": "No fibrous matting fills the space between stubs. The trunk surface between the pegs is bare and smooth (render-2, render-3 vs reference-1, reference-2).", "trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting"}, {"defect": "The trunk is a uniform slate blue-grey. It is not the grey-brown to reddish-brown of the references, and the stub faces are not weathered paler.", "trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering"}, {"defect": "There is no brown-to-grey collar of dead fronds under the living crown. Every hanging frond is the same dark green as the live ones.", "trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt"}, {"defect": "In the P-WHOLE views the fronds read near-black dark green, not blue-green to grey-green. Only the closer render-2 shows sage/grey-green leaflet material.", "trait_id": "frond-colour-range"}], "observations": ["render-0 and render-1 (seeds 1 and 42) show one tall, straight, unbranched trunk with a slight basal flare and a compact crown of roughly 25-35 radiating pinnate fronds.", "The crown is small relative to trunk height, and the fronds stay mostly straight. Reference-0 shows long, strongly recurved fronds forming a dome.", "render-2 shows grey-green/sage leaflet material that looks dark wherever it is shaded. At whole-tree distance the crown reads almost black against the sky.", "render-3 carries visibility 'hidden' in its metadata, but the image clearly shows a close trunk section with rounded cylindrical pegs. It was assessed from the image as shown.", "The trunk pegs are leaf-base stubs from the trunk organs. They are not branches or epiphytes, so the trunk counts as bare and unbranched.", "fruit-clusters-pendent is a known gap (fn-111) and was not assessed.", "The spruce anchor was used only for finish level. The render's finish is comparable, but the morphology differences above are defining."], "findings": [{"observation": "Fronds radiate from a single apex like straight spokes with little recurve. The crown outline is a round starburst, not an arching hemisphere or shuttlecock, and the lowest fronds hang vertically tight to the trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and droop/curvature may be too low relative to the stiff rachis. This is not established.", "trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds"}, {"observation": "Leaflets are short lanceolate blades spaced sparsely along each rachis. Each frond reads thin and see-through, unlike the dense, long leaflets in reference-0 and reference-1.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Leaflet size and density dials may still be low. The owner named leaflet size as the first dial.", "trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds"}, {"observation": "Leaflets are narrow, pointed and rigid, set at varied angles, and give a bristly frond margin in silhouette.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow"}, {"observation": "The trunk is smooth with sparse cylindrical, round-capped pegs. The references show a dense spiral diamond lattice of flat-faced wedge stubs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The stub organ's density, cross-section and phyllotaxis packing may not yet tessellate. This is not established.", "trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern"}, {"observation": "No fibre or husk fills the space between stubs, and the trunk surface is bare.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting"}, {"observation": "There is one unbranched columnar stem with near-constant diameter. It is straight and vertical with no waviness, which matches reference-1 and reference-2 and the owner's requirement.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem"}, {"observation": "The trunk is straight and vertical. Reference-0's lean and S-curve is recorded variation, and the owner wants straight or gently leaning.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve"}, {"observation": "Nothing but leaf-base stubs grows on the trunk: no epiphytes, vines or foliage. The green column on the upper trunk is consistent with the lowest crown fronds hanging down.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk"}, {"observation": "In the P-WHOLE views the fronds read near-black dark green. The grey-green material shows only up close in render-2.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Backlighting, or the shaded undersides of sparse leaflets, may darken the whole-view reading.", "trait_id": "frond-colour-range"}, {"observation": "There is no brown or grey dead-frond collar under the living crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt"}, {"observation": "The trunk is a uniform slate blue-grey, not grey-brown to reddish-brown, and the stub faces are not weathered paler.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering"}, {"observation": "The trunk widens into a flared base at the ground, consistent with reference-0.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "basal-flare"}, {"observation": "No smooth crownshaft is visible. The frond bases sit directly on the trunk top.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent"}, {"observation": "Fruit clusters are absent. This is a known gap (fn-111) and was not assessed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent"}, {"observation": "render-3 metadata says visibility 'hidden', but the image shows the stubs clearly. It was assessed as shown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern"}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The fronds are pinnate and radiate from one apex, but they are straight, short and sparse, not long and arching. The outline reads as a starburst, not a drooping dome."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Leaflets are narrow, pointed and stiff at varied angles, with a bristly margin. Their shortness is covered under the crown finding."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The render has sparse cylindrical pegs on a smooth trunk, with no tessellating lattice of wedge stubs."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "There is no fibre between the stubs; the trunk surface is smooth."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "One unbranched, straight stem of near-constant diameter."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Known gap (fn-111); not assessed."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "There is no brown dead-frond collar; every hanging frond is green."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The trunk is slate blue-grey, not grey-brown to reddish-brown, with no weathered stub faces."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The trunk flares at the ground."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The whole-tree views read near-black green, not the blue-green to grey-green the owner requires."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "No crownshaft is drawn."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2"], "explanation": "The trunk is bare, as the owner requires. The epiphytes in the references are scene variation."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"c947ec19-270a-4318-95a5-fd1b6ed32138","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5-5","permissionMode":"defau